andling reporter-requested metadata.\n\nPreserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9376-fails-native-image-run-org.eclipse.jetty-jetty-http-10.0.0-a46efba8\n\nMost likely cause: test-version resolution is inconsistent. The workflow correctly selected the shared `9.4.1.v20170120` test project and generated `PreEncodedHttpFieldTest.java` there, but all three `generateMetadata` attempts looked for `tests/src/org.eclipse.jetty/jetty-http/10.0.0/build.gradle` and failed because it does not exist. The generated test was therefore never compiled or run. Metrics confirm failure after 3 iterations, zero generated LOC recorded, no metadata artifact, and identical starting/ending commits. The preceding `fixTestNativeImageRun` task succeeded, while dynamic-access reporting failed because `build/native/nativeTestCompile/dynamic-access` was not produced.\n\nInspect:\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http:10.0.0/issue-requested-metadata/pi-generation-2026-09-29T10-27-14-832451Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http:10.0.0/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-29T10-23-29-909842Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http:10.0.0/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-09-29T10-20-16-826899Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Correct or work around coordinate-to-test-project resolution so metadata generation for `10.0.0` uses the shared `9.4.1.v20170120` test suite.\n2. Review and run the preserved `PreEncodedHttpFieldTest.java`, then rerun metadata generation and the full coordinate test.\n3. If dynamic-access coverage is still unavailable, investigate why Native Image produced no `dynamic-access` directory and verify the Jetty transitive metadata versions used by the test.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b79734ee4cf6a65016abb937602dc87d29f016483306c5b1f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-cod